THOUGHT: The FIELD_NO_INIT error is because `CubemapLoaderInfo.data` is non-null by default under NullAway’s rules but is not initialized in the constructor. It’s also potentially left unassigned in `loadAsync` when the file is not KTX and `parameter` is null or has `cubemapData == null`. To satisfy NullAway and avoid NPEs, I should (1) mark `data` as `@Nullable` and (2) guard all uses of `info.data` with null checks, returning early from `loadSync` if `data` is null. I’ll update the field declaration and add a null check before `info.data.isPrepared()` in `loadAsync`, and before using `info.data` in `loadSync`. Then I’ll run the Gradle compile to confirm the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '46s/CubemapData data;/@Nullable CubemapData data;/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/assets/loaders/CubemapLoader.java && sed -i '81s/.*/    if (info.data != null && !info.data.isPrepared()) info.data.prepare();/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/assets/loaders/CubemapLoader.java && sed -i '91,97c\    if (info == null || info.data == null) return null;
    Cubemap cubemap = info.cubemap;
    if (cubemap != null) {
      cubemap.load(info.data);
    } else {
      cubemap = new Cubemap(info.data);
    }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/assets/loaders/CubemapLoader.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1
```

